# Cursor AI Rules for IDEAI Monorepo

## Code Standards

### Code Headers
All code files must include rich, descriptive headers with:
- @fileoverview: Brief description
- @module: Module name
- @description: Detailed explanation
- @example: Usage examples
- @see: Related files
- @todo: Known issues or improvements

### Code Quality
- TypeScript strict mode
- All functions typed
- No `any` types
- Error handling for async operations
- Comments for complex logic

## Commit Standards

### Commit Messages
All commits must be detailed:
```
type(scope): detailed subject line

Detailed explanation of what changed and why.

- Specific change 1
- Specific change 2
- Specific change 3
```

### Commit Signing in Non-Interactive Environment
**CRITICAL**: When committing in Cursor/AI tools (non-interactive):
1. Disable auto-sign: `git config --global --unset commit.gpgsign`
2. Make commit
3. Re-enable: `git config --global commit.gpgsign true`

This is required because GPG signing needs passphrase entry, which isn't possible in non-interactive environments.

## Documentation Standards

### OCD Accuracy Required
Every documentation commit must ensure:
- 100% accuracy - all information current and correct
- All code examples tested and working
- All file paths verified (relative paths correct)
- All version numbers current
- All links tested and working
- All cross-references updated
- Terminology consistent
- No outdated information
- No broken references
- Status information accurate

### Documentation Review Before Commit
- [ ] All code examples work
- [ ] All paths correct
- [ ] All links work
- [ ] All versions current
- [ ] All references updated
- [ ] No outdated info
- [ ] Consistent terminology

## CI/CD Standards

### All CI/CD Must Be Respected
Before committing:
- [ ] `pnpm lint` passes
- [ ] `pnpm check-types` passes
- [ ] `pnpm build` succeeds
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] No console errors

Never skip CI checks. All PRs must pass CI before merge.

## Workflow

1. Make changes
2. Run checks: `pnpm lint && pnpm check-types && pnpm build`
3. Update documentation if code changed (ensure OCD accuracy)
4. Write detailed commit message
5. If in non-interactive environment, disable auto-sign, commit, re-enable
6. Push and verify CI passes

